  "text_pages": [
    "Closing Remarks by Ms. Nguyễn Thị Yến Nhi (Mia) Executive Committee Member, DNTU Buddies Team Closing Ceremony of the 54th PAS Program at DNTU\nStaff & Faculty\nStudents\nAdmissions – Search\nGreen DNTU\n360 campus\n15:25 - 22-07-2026\n54\nINTERNATIONAL COOPERATION\nClosing Remarks by Ms. Nguyễn Thị Yến Nhi (Mia) Executive Committee Member, DNTU Buddies Team Closing Ceremony of the 54th PAS Program at DNTU\nClosing Remarks by Ms. Nguyễn Thị Yến Nhi (Mia)\nExecutive Committee Member, DNTU Buddies Team\nClosing Ceremony of the 54th PAS Program at DNTU\nGood afternoon, distinguished professors, respected lecturers, dear members of the PAS Team, fellow DNTU students, ladies and gentlemen.\nMy name is\nNguyễn Thị Yến Nhi\n, a third-year student majoring in Oriental Studies at the Faculty of Foreign Languages. However, most of my friends know me by my nickname,\nMia\n. I am also a member of the Executive Committee of the\nDNTU Buddies Team\n. It is truly an honor for me to stand here today and share a few words after completing my role in supporting the\n54th PAS Program at DNTU\n.\nAlthough this is my second time participating as a Buddy, I can still vividly remember the moment we welcomed everyone at the airport just two weeks ago. It feels like only yesterday, yet now we have already reached the time to say goodbye to our dear\nXin Chào Ho\nfamily.\nOver the past two weeks, we have walked this journey together, supporting one another and creating countless unforgettable memories. There are so many special moments that sometimes a single word is enough to bring them all back. For example, if I simply say\n\"Bánh mì,\"\nI'm sure everyone here immediately remembers the stories behind it.\nFrom our classes in rooms G401 and G415, to the International Food Festival, the Sports Festival, volunteer teaching activities for local primary school children, and the many mornings when we woke up very early and the evenings when we returned home very late after spending the entire day together—every experience became a precious memory. Before we even realized it, something as simple as sharing meals together had become one of the moments I will treasure the most.\nMost of the members of Xin Chào Ho are around my age, and some of you are even first-year university students. Although a few of you were not feeling well during the program, you still participated enthusiastically in every activity with positive attitudes and warm smiles. We truly admire your dedication and perseverance.\nYour kindness, enthusiasm, and positive energy brought so much joy to our classrooms, meaningful learning experiences to the children we taught, and unforgettable moments to DNTU students and every member of the DNTU Buddies Team.\nThrough this program, I have not only gained many wonderful friends but also learned valuable lessons about culture, sharing, mutual understanding, and the friendship between Vietnam and Korea.\nTo\nJunhyung, Minha, Hyunseo, Gayeon, Nayeon, Youngeun, Yedam, Yein, Juan, Yoonha, Geonwoo, Seoyeon, Hyungjun, Seokhwan, Jiwoo, Hojeong, Seungchan, Changhoon, Siyeon, and Haein\n—please don't forget my sleepy face every morning... even though, in reality, I was always genuinely happy to see all of you.\nI would also like to express my deepest gratitude to\nProfessor Cho\n.\nProfessor Cho, you have been like a father to all of us throughout this program. Even though we were supposed to be the ones supporting you as our international guest at DNTU, you were always the one quietly looking after us instead. Despite your busy schedule, you always found time to check on us, encourage us, and stand beside the DNTU Buddies Team every single day.\nAll of us sincerely admire and appreciate your kindness, care, and dedication.\nIn Korea, there is a beautiful saying:\n\"옷깃만 스쳐도 전생의 인연이다.\"\nIt means,\n\"Even brushing sleeves with someone is a connection carried over from a previous lifetime.\"\nPerhaps that is why, on the very first day we met, you and the PAS Team gave each of us a PAS T-shirt as a symbol of our new connection.\nToday, on behalf of the DNTU Buddies Team, I would like to present you with a\nDNTU T-shirt\n. We hope it will symbolize our wish that the bond between DNTU, Hoseo University, and all of us will continue to grow stronger for many years to come.\nFinally, I would like to extend my heartfelt best wishes to every member of\nXin Chào Ho\n,\nProfessor Cho\n,\nProfessor Yoon\n, and\nMr. Yoo\n.\nMay all of you always enjoy good health, happiness, and continued success in everything you pursue. We also hope that you will always carry with you wonderful memories of Vietnam, of DNTU, and of the friendships we have built together.\nAlthough today we say goodbye, I truly believe this is not the end of our journey.\nInstead, it is simply another beginning.\nThank you for bringing so much warmth, kindness, laughter, and unforgettable memories to our summer.\nWe sincerely look forward to meeting all of you again in the near future.\nThank you very much!\nHashtag:\nINTERNATIONAL COOPERATION\nRelated Articles\nLecturer at the Faculty of Foreign Languages Represents Vietnam at India’s Republic Day 2025\nCongratulations to DNTU Students Participating in the Exchange Program at Chinese Culture University\nRECEIVING THE P2A PHILIPPINES DELEGATION FOR A VISIT AND WORKING SESSION AT DNTU\nWelcoming UST University Students from Indonesia to DNTU for the Teaching Assistant Program\nWelcoming the Delegation of Leaders, Lecturers, and Students from Nueva Ecija University of Science and Technology, Philippines to the Teaching Assistant Program at DNTU\nĐoàn giảng viên DNTU tham gia Chương trình Tập huấn Chuyên ngành Kỹ thuật tại Trường Đại học Kỹ thuật và Công nghệ nghề nghiệp Sơn Đông, Trung Quốc\nSinh viên Trường Đại học Công nghệ Đồng Nai tham gia Giao lưu văn hóa và học thuật tại Trường Đại học Kỹ thuật và Công nghệ Nghề nghiệp Sơn Đông, Trung Quốc\nĐón tiếp đoàn đại diện trường Đại học Kyonggi, Hàn Quốc: Thúc đẩy hợp tác và mở rộng cơ hội học tập cho sinh viên\nChào đón đoàn giảng viên, sinh viên Trường Đại học Nueva Ecija, Philippines đến giao lưu và học tập tại DNTU\nLễ đón tiếp và ký kết MOU giữa Trường Đại học Công nghệ Đồng Nai và Trường Đại học Kỹ thuật và Công nghệ Nghề nghiệp Sơn Đông, Trung Quốc\nDong Nai Technology University\nContact:\nEmail: info@dntu.edu.vn\nPhone: 0904 39 7733\nSocial network:\nBRIGHTING UP THE FACULTY OF ENGINEERING – CONGRATULATIONS TO TWO OUTSTANDING STUDENTS ON RECEIVING THE INTERNATIONAL SCHOLARSHIP TO COMMTECH CAMP HIGHLIGHT 2026!\nINTERNATIONAL COOPERATION\nDNTU STUDENTS READY TO CONQUER THE ASEAN AI HACKATHON 2026 GRAND FINALE!\nINTERNATIONAL COOPERATION\nDNTU FOOD TECHNOLOGY STUDENT SUCCESSFULLY COMPLETES INTERNSHIP AT CHINESE CULTURE UNIVERSITY (CCU)\nINTERNATIONAL COOPERATION\nDONG NAI TECHNOLOGY UNIVERSITY EXPANDING CLEAR PATHWAYS FOR TRANSFER AND STUDY IN KOREA WITH CHOSUN UNIVERSITY\nINTERNATIONAL COOPERATION\nDONG NAI TECHNOLOGY UNIVERSITY EXPANDING ACADEMIC AND CULTURAL EXCHANGE WITH JEONJU UNIVERSITY\nDNTU STUDENTS DEPART FOR A ONE-YEAR INTERNATIONAL INTERNSHIP PROGRAM IN TAIWAN\nDNTU Student Successfully Completes International Internship at Renaissance Harbour View Hotel Hong Kong\nDNTU INVITES THE UNIVERSITY COMMUNITY TO SUPPORT ITS TEAM IN THE P2A HACKATHON AI 2026\nDNTU WELCOMES CHINESE EDUCATION EXPERTS TO ADVANCE INTERNATIONAL COLLABORATION AND GLOBAL ENGAGEMENT\nCopyright © 2026 - DNTU\nTrong suốt hai thập kỷ xây dựng và phát triển một hành trình vẻ vang và đầy tự hào, Trường Đại học Công nghệ Đồng Nai không ngừng theo đuổi sự đổi mới sáng tạo thông qua hệ thống giáo dục toàn diện.\nLooking for a reliable resource to download, analyze, or research legendary and modern web shells?\nphpshells.net\noffers the most trusted underground archive for php shell tools, bypass scripts, file managers, and symlink shells—perfect for redteam, pentest, and cybersecurity professionals seeking the latest in web shell technology."
